{title: I Need the Every Hour}
{artist: Annie S. Hawks}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
I [G]need Thee every hour, most [C]gracious [G]Lord;
No [D7]tender voice like [G]Thine can [A7]peace [D7]afford.

{comment: Chorus}
I [G]need Thee, O I [D7]need Thee;
Every hour I [G]need Thee;
O [C]bless me now, my [G]Saviour,
I come [D7]to [G]Thee.

{comment: Verse 2}
I need Thee every hour, stay Thou nearby;
Temptations lose their power when Thou art nigh.

{comment: Verse 3}
I need Thee every hour, in joy or pain;
Come quickly and abide, or life is in vain.

{comment: Verse 4}
I need Thee every hour; teach me Thy will;
And Thy rich promises in me fulfill.

{comment: Verse 5}
I need Thee every hour, most Holy One;
O make me Thine indeed, Thou bless'd Son.
